                    <occupation>OCCUPATION</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Ed Pope notes: 2.11.1795 baron d'Ahlberg at Richard Johnson's In Godwin's
                            1796 list as Dahlberg crossed out Co-adjutor of Mentz and Worms along
                            with Prince Bishop of Constanz, was appointed by German diet in Nov 1794
                            to negotiate armistice with France, said in August 1796 to be at Geneva
                            and in March 1798 at Vienna, hoping to become Archbishop of Vienna
                            (British newspapers) 1744 -1817 (Deutsche Biographisch Enzyklopade)
                            Archbishop of Mainz, of Regensburg, Grand Duke of Frankfurt 1810-13
                            under Napoleon. Doesn't mention his English visit but says he was
                            friends with Goethe, Schiller etc.</p>
                    </note>
